# Lesson 05: The .NET Execution & Runtime Engine

Mastering C# requires understanding how the .NET execution engine operates under the hood. While Lesson 04 introduced the high-level architecture, this lesson examines the runtime components in detail: execution environments, memory management, assemblies, type standards, and managed vs. unmanaged execution.

