## 3. Direct Component Mapping

| Acronym | Full Name | Primary Responsibility |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **CLR** | Common Language Runtime | Virtual execution engine, thread management, exception handling, and GC[cite: 10]. |
| **CTS** | Common Type System | Universal data type definition rules across all .NET languages[cite: 10]. |
| **CLS** | Common Language Specification | Rules guaranteeing cross-language interoperability[cite: 10]. |
| **GC** | Garbage Collector | Automatic heap memory reclamation using a 3-generation collection algorithm[cite: 10]. |
| **JIT** | Just-In-Time Compiler | Runtime translation of CIL bytecode into native CPU instructions[cite: 8, 10]. |
| **BCL** | Base Class Library | Fundamental standard primitives (`System.*`)[cite: 10]. |
| **FCL** | Framework Class Library | Comprehensive superset containing the BCL plus UI, Web, and ORM frameworks. |

---

## 4. Key Takeaways

* **Managed Code** executes under the supervision of the **CLR**, which handles memory management (via the **GC**), type verification, and runtime compilation (via the **JIT**)[cite: 8, 10].
* The **CTS** standardizes data types, while the **CLS** guarantees cross-language interoperability rules[cite: 10].
* An **Assembly** is a self-describing compiled binary containing **CIL bytecode**, **Metadata**, and an assembly **Manifest**[cite: 8].
* **FCL** is the complete toolkit containing the fundamental **BCL** plus domain-specific application frameworks.
